# Supplemental native UIA evidence packet assembler

This external draft creates a new `../native-uia-supplement-packet-20260930/`
after the long A-B-B-A driver has finished and restored both checkouts. It
refuses to overwrite any existing packet. Run after reviewing the completed
long evidence:

```powershell
py -3 C:/RedSalamander.Perf/evidence/i26-ui/native-uia-supplement-driver-20260930/build_packet.py
```

The assembler verifies the CI49 completed run, all 122 suite receipts against
their root hashes and raw logs, all eight consumer receipts, both positive ASan
probes and the x64/ARM64 audits. It requires the three ARM64 Menu receipts to
retain their nine interactive-desktop skips and does not describe those cases
as executed. It also requires all eight short crossover receipts and their
original comparison sidecars, the reviewed short assessment, and a completed
long driver result with all receipts, pair comparisons, stock comparator
rejections, source restoration and original-binary rebuild records.

It packages every selected evidence file using the earlier packet's
`original-file-map.json` and short content-hash `raw/*.receipt` layout, then
copies the same `Verify-Packet.ps1` and writes `SHA256SUMS` for exact membership.
CI `run-progress.json` and `run-latest.json` are excluded because the completed
run record supersedes them. Binaries, archives, dependency trees and node
outputs are excluded; CI gallery PNG/HTML files remain as visual evidence.

The packet preserves performance flags; it does not declare a performance
pass. The long fixture measures offscreen WARP frames, not WindowHost UIA
operations or presented FPS. The x64 audit was recorded before the overall CI
workflow completed, so its earlier in-progress marker remains as provenance
alongside the final run and ARM64 audit. The packet has no repository writes.
